---
description: Update canonical docs in the same change when documented behaviour changes; follow Diátaxis
alwaysApply: true
---

Documentation in this repository follows the official Diátaxis method:

https://diataxis.fr/start-here/

Diátaxis has exactly four documentation types: Tutorials, How-to guides, Reference, and Explanation.
Repository areas such as `docs/current-state/`, `docs/decisions/`, and `docs/archive/` are lifecycle/governance folders, not additional Diátaxis types.

When unsure how to classify or structure a documentation change, consult the official Diátaxis site (start-here and compass) before inventing a new category or mixing types unnecessarily.
Use `docs/README.md` as the authoritative in-repo documentation map and authority model.

If an implementation change alters approved behavior, architecture, API usage, routes, schemas, or UX, update the affected canonical documentation in the same change.

Do not edit docs for implementation-only changes that do not affect documented behavior.

Remove stale statements caused by the change before completion.

Do not rewrite `docs/archive/**`.
